{\pard \par}{\pard{\i Note.} A significant {\i b}-weight indicates the beta-weight and semi-partial correlation are also significant. {\i b} represents unstandardized regression weights. {\i beta} indicates the standardized regression weights. {\i sr\super 2\nosupersub} represents the semi-partial correlation squared. {\i r} represents the zero-order correlation. {\i LL} and {\i UL} indicate the lower and upper limits of a confidence interval, respectively.\line * indicates {\i p} < .05. ** indicates {\i p} < .01.\par}
}
